   * admin link carried the attribute, was never un-hidden by the claim check,
   * and was on screen for every signed-in member anyway (2026-09-03, Josh:
   * "Admin console only shows up for people with permission"). Harmless in
   * itself — /admin gates itself — but it advertised a door nobody could open.
   *
   * The same silence was defeating the upload queue's row controls, which is
   * where it actually cost something: `.gallery-thumb-remove` and
   * `.gallery-tools` both set `display: flex`, so every row showed its Cancel
   * AND its Retry/Dismiss pair at once, on rows that had nothing to retry.
   * (VisualNeedsSelector already knew — it ships its own
   * `visual-needs-selector[hidden]` rule for exactly this reason.)
   *
   * Astro's scope attribute lifts this to (0,2,0) and `!important` settles the
   * ties with the component's own classes, so from here `hidden` means hidden.
   * Same trap, same fix as `.ccard--preview [hidden]` in communityCard.css.
   */
  [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /*
